SYNC(1)                        P32W Unix                         SYNC(1)

NAME
       sync - write the cached blocks to the disk

SYNOPSIS
       sync

DESCRIPTION
       sync calls sync(2): every modified block in the kernel's
       buffer cache, and every changed inode and superblock, is
       written to its device (the CompactFlash card /dev/disk, or
       /dev/ram). Run it before taking out the card or switching
       off without halt(1) or shutdown(1), which do it themselves.

EXIT STATUS
       0.

SEE ALSO
       sync(2), halt(1), shutdown(1), df(1), fsck(8)

BUGS
       Data still buffered inside a running program (stdio) is not
       the kernel's to write. The filesystem is not marked clean;
       only halt, reboot and shutdown do that.
